Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.01,0:00:38.02,sign_song_op_1206,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,500)\an7\pos(263,200)\fs14\blur0.2}Song by Niihama Leon
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.59,0:00:51.32,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,Unquenchable love is the fuse!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.32,0:00:53.81,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,These detective skills are on fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.81,0:00:55.74,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,A detective falls in moonlit darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.74,0:00:57.76,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,The boys get fired up\Nwhile the girls are away!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.76,0:00:59.62,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,Always determining the one truth
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.62,0:01:01.43,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,with the body of a child\Nand the mind of an adult,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.43,0:01:04.02,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,his name is Detective Conan!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.13,0:02:36.01,sign_episode_title,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fad(400,1)}Girls Day Mystery 5\N(Part One)
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.25,0:02:33.57,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,"Girls Day Mystery 5, Part One!"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.01,0:02:39.01,sign_1220_wedding_hall,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(500,90)\yshad3\fscx85\an2\frz2\fnGeorgia}KOIKE GARDEN WEDDING HALL
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.79,0:02:45.43,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Well, now that I just {\i1}happened{\i0}\Nto come across this case...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.43,0:02:48.02,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I can't very well ignore it, now can I?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.30,0:02:51.53,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Seriously, we {\i0}happen{\i1} to\Ncome across way too many cases.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.53,0:02:55.65,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,We appreciate having\Nyour help again, Mori-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.65,0:03:01.04,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,It might seem at a glance that he may\Nhave drowned, but his neck is broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.30,0:03:05.54,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,This seems to be a murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.54,0:03:06.79,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Seriously...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.51,0:03:13.16,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Wedding halls are\Nsupposed to be happy places.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.16,0:03:16.18,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Why did he have to be\Nmurdered {\i1}here{\i0} of all places?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.61,0:03:21.14,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I don't know the answer to that,\Nbut I do know one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.14,0:03:22.18,DCMain,ALL,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.52,0:03:26.69,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,His name was Mihashi Iwao.\NHe was a detective.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.69,0:03:29.69,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(328,256)}Mihashi Iwao (36)
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.69,0:03:29.69,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fs14\pos(328,273)}Detective
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.32,0:03:40.12,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Like you said, the victim's\Nname was Mihashi Iwao-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.12,0:03:42.45,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,He worked as a detective in Haido City.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.45,0:03:44.95,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,1)}Cause of death was\Na cervical vertebral fracture.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.50,0:03:50.26,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,The estimated time of death is\Nbetween midnight and one last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.72,0:03:53.23,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,No signs of a struggle in the area.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.72,0:03:59.25,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,We believe someone surprised him\Nfrom behind, and broke his neck.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.98,0:04:04.25,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Detective Mihashi\Ndidn't investigate cases;
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.25,0:04:08.35,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,he specialized in investigating\Ninfidelity and backgrounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.69,0:04:10.60,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Did you know him?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.60,0:04:13.65,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Not really. We were only acquaintances.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.65,0:04:19.36,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I'm just familiar with\Nthe other detectives in my area.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.36,0:04:22.46,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,He seemed rather fit.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.46,0:04:24.95,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Yeah. He had a black belt in judo.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.95,0:04:29.37,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,He was once recognized by the police\Nfor apprehending a molester.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.75,0:04:34.26,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Which means he must've\Nbeen a strong person.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.62,0:04:38.88,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Mori-san, do you know anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.88,0:04:40.13,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.13,0:04:44.14,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Then let's go talk to the person\Nwho discovered the body.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.89,0:04:52.40,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(328,255)\fad(500,500)}Manabe Katsuji (19)
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.89,0:04:52.40,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(328,272)\fad(500,500)\fs14}Part-Time Worker
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.08,0:04:53.06,DCMainTop,MANABE,0,0,0,,I arrived at work, got changed, and\Nwent out to tidy up the garden as usual.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.06,0:04:55.27,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,That's when I saw a body\Nfloating in the lake.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.81,0:05:00.53,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,So I avoided touching anything and\Nreported it to the police right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.88,0:05:03.91,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Did you know the victim?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.91,0:05:09.91,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,No. It's not like I could recognize\Na face-down body anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.91,0:05:12.79,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,So you weren't acquainted with him?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.79,0:05:16.96,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,Of course not.\NI just work here part-time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.96,0:05:20.34,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Did anyone else approach the body?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.70,0:05:25.47,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,No. I diligently kept an eye on\Nthe body after I called the police.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.05,0:05:32.60,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,We didn't find a wallet, notebook,\Nphone, or any personal items.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.88,0:05:35.73,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,The culprit must've taken them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.73,0:05:39.17,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Were they trying to conceal his identity?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.17,0:05:40.91,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,We don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.91,0:05:46.62,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,But since they're all missing,\Nthat may have been their intention.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.95,0:05:49.12,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,What should we do, Mori-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.99,0:05:52.98,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Let's check out Mihashi's office.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.33,0:05:56.50,sign_1220_agency_mihashi,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an4\move(275,340,275,115)\yshad2\xshad-2\fry25\frz-12\fax0.3}\hMIHASHI DETECTIVE AGENCY\h
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.46,0:05:59.51,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,This is it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.13,0:06:01.42,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Hey, mister!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.04,0:06:03.05,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,The lock!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.05,0:06:03.98,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.87,0:06:15.99,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,The room's been ransacked.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.54,0:06:18.45,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,I'll go check the other rooms.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.45,0:06:19.45,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.25,0:06:24.45,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,The computer's been destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.25,0:06:30.45,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Files on cases Mihashi investigated\Nare strewn across the floor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.25,0:06:28.20,sign_1220_report,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\frz-14\fs9\fscx90\fax-0.1\an2\bord2\move(540,150,480,150)}MIHASHI DETECTIVE AGENCY\NINVESTIGATIVE REPORT
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.20,0:06:30.45,sign_1220_report,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(365,55)\frz-24\fax-0.1}MIHASHI DETECTIVE AGENCY\NINVESTIGATIVE REPORT
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.41,0:06:35.66,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,The computer's completely broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.83,0:06:41.55,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,The culprit killed Detective Mihashi\Nand ransacked his office.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.55,0:06:44.47,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,What does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.76,0:06:49.49,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,The culprit is trying to\Nhide evidence, which means...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.03,0:06:53.10,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Nobody's in the other rooms, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.43,0:06:59.48,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Does that mean the culprit\Nalready achieved their goal?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.48,0:07:01.80,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Yeah, in all likelihood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.80,0:07:03.52,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Hey, look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.39,0:07:07.99,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I think this is what the culprit\Nwas trying to hide.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.57,0:07:13.23,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Is that an investigative file?\NBut it's been balled up and burned.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.76,0:07:17.12,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,It's useless to us now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.12,0:07:19.08,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I wouldn't say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.75,0:07:28.76,sign_1220_burnt_paper,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\bord3\3c&H868B8F&\fs20\an2\frz-211\fax-0.2\c&H000000&\b0\fad(1000,1)\pos(361,63)}NOVEMBER 11TH
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.13,0:07:25.57,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I can't tell exactly what it says,\Nbut there's a date here.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.57,0:07:28.76,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,November 11th, 20 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.76,0:07:33.81,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Knowing that date\Ndoesn't tell us anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.81,0:07:35.59,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I wouldn't be so sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.60,0:07:47.16,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,You can look up old\Nnewspapers here, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.16,0:07:50.66,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I bet Detective Mihashi came here, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.66,0:07:54.91,sign_1220_spreadsheet,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\frz-3\an3\pos(445,80)\fscx90}\h\h\hTIME\hUSED\h\h\h|\h\h\h\h\hNAME\h\h\h\h\h|\h\h\hNOTE\h\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.58,0:07:58.67,sign_1220_spreadsheet,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an4\fs14\alphaFF\t(1000,1300,\alphaFF,\alpha00)\bord0\pos(470,152)}MIHASHI\NIWAO
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.89,0:08:04.86,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,Here are the newspaper archives.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.86,0:08:07.17,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,Let's look at the ones from 20 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.17,0:08:08.80,sign_1220_newspaper_online,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an9\fnImpact\pos(333,95)\fad(500,1)\3c&H6B3E30&\c&HDED3CE&}NICHIURI NEWS{\fs10\c&H6B3E30&\3c&HDED4CF&}\N\NThree Companies\NIntroduce\NNew Cell Phones
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.80,0:08:12.79,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,What's this?\NAre you saying this is a clue?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.79,0:08:16.18,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Detective Chiba, could you\Nlook up other articles, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.18,0:08:17.43,DCMain,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,10)\alpha00\fad(1,1)\fscx100\fscy100\p1\shad0\bord3\c&HFEFEFE&\3c&H846049&}m 150 00 l 00 00 00 185 150 185
Dialogue: 1,0:08:16.18,0:08:17.43,sign_1220_phone_messages_bubble,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,10)\fs12\bord0\shad0\fnTrebuchet MS\3c&HF4F0EE&}\h\N\hMORI KOGORO\N\N\h\h{\bord2}What's this? Are you{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}saying this is a clue?{\bord0}\h\h\N\N\N\N\hEDOGAWA CONAN\h\N\N\h\h{\bord2}Detective Chiba,{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}could you look up{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}other articles, too?{\bord0}\h\h\N\N\N\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\alphaFF\t(400,600,\alphaFF,\alpha00)}CHIBA KAZUNOBU\h\N\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\bord2}Got it.{\bord0}\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.43,0:08:17.47,sign_1220_newspaper_online,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an9\fnImpact\pos(333,95)\3c&H6B3E30&\c&HDED3CE&}NICHIURI NEWS{\fs10\c&H6B3E30&\3c&HDED4CF&}\N\NThree Companies\NIntroduce\NNew Cell Phones
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.47,0:08:19.44,sign_1220_newspaper_online,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an9\fnTimes New Roman\b1\fscx80\pos(345,95)\fad(1,1)\c&H6B3E30&\3c&HC3B3A9&}MILLIONAIRE'S\NSON MURDERED
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.44,0:08:22.66,DCItalic,TAKAGI/ID,0,0,0,,The son of a millionaire was murdered?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.06,0:08:24.82,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,It's about a murder case.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.25,0:08:27.30,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,"Before dawn on the 11th,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.30,0:08:32.28,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,a gruesome murder took place\Nat a home in Beika City.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.98,0:08:34.88,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,The victims were Koike Seiji,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.88,0:08:39.39,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,the son of millionaire and\Nbusinessman Koike Tatsuya,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.39,0:08:45.03,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,as well as their butler Hamano Shogo\Nand maid Mishima Kyoko-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.72,0:08:49.65,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,The culprit used branch-cutters\Nthat were in the yard
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.65,0:08:54.57,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,to brutally kill all three\Nvictims before fleeing.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.96,0:09:00.36,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,The police say they're currently\Ninvestigating exactly what happened."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.10,0:09:04.69,DCMain,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,160)\alpha00\fad(1,1)\fscx100\fscy100\p1\shad0\bord3\c&HFEFEFE&\3c&H000000&}m 150 00 l 00 00 00 110 150 110
Dialogue: 1,0:09:02.10,0:09:04.69,sign_1220_phone_messages_bubble,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,160)\fs12\bord0\shad0\fnTrebuchet MS\3c&HF4F0EE&\c&H000000&}\h\N\hCHIBA KAZUNOBU\h\N\N\h\h{\bord2}Check the local news{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}for November 11th.{\bord0}\h\h\N\N\N\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMORI KOGORO\h\N\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\bord2}What about this case?{\bord0}\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.10,0:09:04.69,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,What about this case?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.69,0:09:10.57,DCMain,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an9\pos(630,10)\alpha00\fad(1,1)\fscx100\fscy100\p1\shad0\bord3\c&HFEFEFE&\3c&H000000&}m 150 00 l 00 00 00 140 150 140
Dialogue: 1,0:09:04.69,0:09:10.57,sign_1220_phone_messages_bubble,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an9\pos(630,10)\fs12\bord0\shad0\fnTrebuchet MS\3c&HF4F0EE&\c&H000000&}\h\N\hMORI KOGORO\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\N\N\h\h{\bord2}What about this case?{\bord0}\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\N\N\N\N\hEDOGAWA CONAN\h\N\N\h\h{\bord2}I don't know yet,{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}but it was a big case.{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}There must be{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}a follow-up article.{\bord0}\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.69,0:09:08.56,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,I don't know yet, but it was a big case.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.56,0:09:10.57,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,There must be a follow-up article.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.78,0:09:12.57,sign_1220_newspaper_online,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(430,131)\an7\3c&H693E31&\c&HF8F8F4&\fnImpact}New Development\Nin Millionaire's\NSon Murder Case
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.41,0:09:12.57,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.87,0:09:18.54,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,"According to the police, the culprit\Nin the millionaire's son murder case
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.54,0:09:23.19,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,was most likely Hayama Taro,\Nthe son of the gardener
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.19,0:09:26.34,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,in the employ of\Nmillionaire Koike Tatsuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.34,0:09:30.29,sign_1220_newspaper_online,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\3c&H693E31&\c&HF8F8F4&\fs38\fnImpact\an9\pos(375,150)\fad(1,1000)}New Development\Nin Millionaire's Son\NMurder Case
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.34,0:09:29.33,DCItalicTop,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,A national search\Nfor the suspect is underway.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.85,0:09:34.72,DCItalicTop,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,The suspect disappeared after the\Nmurders and seems to be on the run."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.09,0:09:34.72,sign_1220_newspaper_online_zoomed,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fad(100,1)\an2\pos(320,320)\bord3\fscx100\fscy100\fs24\3c&HDED3CE&\c&H6B3E30&}Suspect Hayama Taro (20)
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.97,0:09:36.22,sign_1220_newspaper_online_zoomed,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fs30\an5\pos(170,261)\bord7\shad3\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HDED4CF&}Insider Testimony:\NThe Message\NLeft By the Culprit
Dialogue: 1,0:09:34.97,0:09:36.22,sign_1220_newspaper_online_zoomed,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fs30\an5\pos(170,261)\bord4\c&HFFFFFF&}Insider Testimony:\NThe Message\NLeft By the Culprit
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.80,0:09:38.97,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,"The Message Left By the Culprit?"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.54,0:09:46.26,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,"According to an insider, the suspect\Nfrequently said to those around him,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.00,0:09:49.52,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,'Even if I were the moon,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.52,0:09:53.74,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,the moon could become the sun\Nif the sun were destroyed.'"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.07,0:09:56.09,DCItalic,TAKAGI/ID,0,0,0,,The moon and the sun?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.09,0:09:59.12,DCItalic,TAKAGI/ID,0,0,0,,Does that have something\Nto do with this case?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.12,0:10:03.62,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,Like I've been saying, what does\Nthis case have to do with anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.12,0:10:06.50,DCMain,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,10)\alpha00\fad(1,1)\fscx100\fscy100\p1\shad0\bord3\c&HFEFEFE&\3c&H846049&}m 150 00 l 00 00 00 140 150 140
Dialogue: 1,0:10:04.12,0:10:06.50,sign_1220_phone_messages_bubble,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(10,10)\fs12\bord0\shad0\fnTrebuchet MS\3c&HF4F0EE&}\h\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hMORI KOGORO\N\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\bord2}Like I've been saying,{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h\h\h{\bord2}what does this case have{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h{\bord2}to do with anything?{\bord0}\h\h\N\N\N\N\h{\alphaFF\t(0,200,\alphaFF,\alpha00)}EDOGAWA CONAN\h\N\N\h\h{\bord2}Look at the photo{\bord0}\h\h\N\h\h{\bord2}at the bottom!{\bord0}\h\h
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.73,0:10:06.51,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Look at the photo at the bottom!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.25,0:10:10.88,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Haven't we seen this building before?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.28,0:10:12.38,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,This building!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.21,0:10:15.03,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,It's that wedding hall!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.03,0:10:18.64,DCItalic,TAKAGI/ID,0,0,0,,Another murder took place\Nthere in the past!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.00,0:10:21.64,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,Looks like we found the connection.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.15,0:10:30.32,DCItalic,KOGORO/ID,0,0,0,,Let's go question people\Nat the wedding hall again.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.32,0:10:33.23,DCItalic,CHIBA/ID,0,0,0,,I'll return to HQ and\Ndo some more research.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.23,0:10:34.78,DCItalic,TAKAGI/ID,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.78,0:10:36.78,sign_1220_wedding_hall,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\move(355,90,495,90)\yshad3\fscx85\an2\frz2\fnGeorgia}KOIKE GARDEN WEDDING HALL
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.19,0:10:38.78,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,You're back?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.78,0:10:43.04,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Is there anyone who's\Nknowledgeable about this facility?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.04,0:10:47.79,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,We'd like to ask about before\Nit became a wedding hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.79,0:10:51.34,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,In that case, you should\Ntalk to the manager.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.67,0:10:55.97,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,I'm Hamano, the manager.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.97,0:10:59.29,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Do you know how this building\Nbecame a wedding hall
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.29,0:11:03.43,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,or about the incident that\Nhappened 20 years ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.68,0:11:08.19,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,255)\fad(500,500)}Hamano Kozo (54)
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.68,0:11:08.19,sign_suspect,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,272)\fad(500,500)\fs14}Wedding Hall Manager
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.68,0:11:08.57,DCMainTop,HAMANO,0,0,0,,Of course I do.\NThat's how I lost my uncle.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.96,0:11:11.44,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,You're familiar with the case?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.44,0:11:12.63,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.63,0:11:15.81,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,The Koikes who owned this building
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.81,0:11:18.73,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,were one of Japan's most\Ndistinguished families.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.73,0:11:25.88,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,They lost their only heir,\NSeiji-san, in that tragic incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.88,0:11:33.26,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,I heard they couldn't remain at this\Nmansion, where the tragedy took place.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.67,0:11:40.18,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,They didn't want this beautiful structure\Nto end as a place of sadness,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.18,0:11:42.74,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,so once things had cooled down\Nseveral years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.74,0:11:47.44,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,it was turned into a wedding hall.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.56,0:11:51.46,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,If you'd like to know more...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.89,0:11:56.57,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,Here's the key to the reference room.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.40,0:11:56.57,sign_1220_key_reference_room,SIGN KEY,0,0,0,,{\frz34\fax0.5\an2\fad(700,1)\pos(302,106)}REFERENCE ROOM
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.70,0:12:01.45,sign_1220_door_reference_room,SIGN DOOR,0,0,0,,{\move(320,70,320,143)\an2\frx10\yshad-3\fnGeorgia\c&H544F3B&\3c&HE8FFFD&\4c&H4F90B2&\fs24}Reference Room
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.61,0:12:05.00,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Let's see...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.08,0:12:14.38,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Let's split up and see what we can find.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.38,0:12:15.75,sign_1220_book_names,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an8\frz25\c&H855D4C&\fscx130\pos(348,225)}KOIKE TATSUYA
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.13,0:12:18.38,sign_1220_book_names,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an8\frz25\c&H3A3F40&\blur2\t(0,300,\blur2,\blur0.1)\fscx110\pos(345,219)}KOIKE TATSUYA
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.86,0:12:18.38,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,"Koike Tatsuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.88,0:12:24.60,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,He built his wealth through real estate\Nsales and moved onto the sale of homes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.60,0:12:29.14,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,20 years later, he became one of\NJapan's most prominent millionaires.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.14,0:12:35.56,sign_1220_book_names,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\move(485,220,550,-20,2600,6400)\an8\frz-3}KOIKE TOSHIKO-SAN
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.43,0:12:33.44,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,He and his wife Toshiko-san\Nhad been friends since childhood,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.44,0:12:37.53,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,and everyone believed their marriage\Nwas a foregone conclusion."
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.94,0:12:43.85,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,This mansion was originally built during\Nthe Edo Period as a samurai residence.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.85,0:12:48.30,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,After succeeding in business,\NKoike Tatsuya bought it
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.30,0:12:51.50,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,and spent a fortune remodeling it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.42,0:12:56.92,sign_1220_book_names_photo,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(371,305)\frz-5\fax-0.2}KOIKE FAMILY GROUP PHOTO
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.41,0:13:01.23,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,In any case, this is a {\i1}ton{\i0} of dust.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.23,0:13:06.93,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,It's no surprise. I doubt anyone\Nlooks at these documents often.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.85,0:13:13.77,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I feel like staying in this moldy room\Nany longer will make me sick.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.04,0:13:19.71,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,It doesn't just smell like mold.\NIt smells burnt—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.71,0:13:21.20,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,Fire!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.95,0:13:36.46,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.40,0:13:41.72,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Don't waste any time! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.50,0:13:46.22,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,No good. It's a dead end.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.22,0:13:47.35,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,This way!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.05,0:13:51.10,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Hey, kid!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.10,0:13:53.10,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I'll be okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.10,0:13:56.02,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,At this rate, we'll {\i0}all{\i1} be in danger.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.32,0:14:01.40,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.82,0:14:08.91,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Go!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.61,0:14:17.76,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.68,0:14:25.01,DCMain,HAMANO,0,0,0,,The documents...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.97,0:14:30.68,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,The documents were burned.\NAnything that survived is soaked.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.68,0:14:34.75,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,They're lucky the whole place\Ndidn't burn down.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.75,0:14:38.09,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,But this will hinder the investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.09,0:14:39.57,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,That's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.95,0:14:42.02,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,My best suit is ruined.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.92,0:14:44.70,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,Why was there a fire?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.70,0:14:46.40,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,Ow...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.40,0:14:47.98,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,It was probably the culprit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.04,0:14:53.79,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,They set the fire\Nto impede the investigation.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.79,0:14:56.25,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,They really are a nuisance.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.25,0:14:59.17,DCMain,MANABE,0,0,0,,Who commits arson after\Ncommitting a murder?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.69,0:15:01.98,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Detective Chiba.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.98,0:15:04.30,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,I'm glad everyone's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.30,0:15:06.91,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Really, that was a close call.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.91,0:15:10.93,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Yeah, seriously, too close for comfort.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.93,0:15:12.81,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Chiba, you found new info?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.09,0:15:19.53,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Yes. I looked into that 20-year-old\Ncase and learned a few things.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.28,0:15:26.84,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Two years after the case, the suspect\Nwas found in Ishikawa Prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.16,0:15:28.37,DCFlashback,POLICE A,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.37,0:15:30.57,DCFlashback,POLICE B,0,0,0,,How far do you plan to run?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.49,0:15:34.33,DCFlashback,POLICE A,0,0,0,,Don't worry. There's a cliff up ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.33,0:15:37.48,DCFlashback,POLICE B,0,0,0,,So Hayama has nowhere to run.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.25,0:15:40.51,DCFlashback,POLICE A,0,0,0,,Let's hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.51,0:15:41.59,DCFlashback,POLICE B,0,0,0,,Right!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.80,0:15:46.34,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,The police cornered Hayama on a cliff.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.15,0:15:50.72,DCFlashback,POLICE A,0,0,0,,Hayama, give it up!\NThere's nowhere to run!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.45,0:15:57.73,DCFlashback,HAYAMA,0,0,0,,Even if the moon breaks,\Na new moon will take its place!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.52,0:16:14.95,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Those were his last words\Nbefore he jumped off the cliff.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.19,0:16:20.17,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,His body was never found in the sea.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.17,0:16:24.72,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Then it's possible he escaped.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.72,0:16:27.33,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,It's hard to believe the culprit survived
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.33,0:16:30.80,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,after leaping into the rough\Nwaters of the Sea of Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.18,0:16:33.78,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,There were no records\Nof the culprit being seen
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.78,0:16:37.43,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,or causing any other\Nincidents after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.43,0:16:41.56,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Detective Chiba,\Nwhat was the culprit like?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.94,0:16:44.21,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Hayama was 20 years old at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.66,0:16:50.82,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,He was the son of the mansion's gardener,\Nand he helped his father with his work.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.74,0:16:58.08,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,He'd never been well-behaved, and\Nhe didn't associate much with others.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.08,0:17:01.83,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,So he was a poorly behaved\Nkid who finally blew up.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.23,0:17:06.66,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Most of the statements\Nabout him were negative.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.02,0:17:12.22,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,But one person spoke in his defense.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.54,0:17:15.38,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,They said they could see\Nhow he could get desperate
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.38,0:17:18.41,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,after being forced\Ninto an environment like that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.41,0:17:19.98,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Who was that person?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.58,0:17:25.05,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,A woman who lived and\Nworked at the mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.05,0:17:25.98,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Hey.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.98,0:17:29.63,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Tell us about the victims instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.63,0:17:33.41,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Why did the gardener's son\Nhave to kill them?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.86,0:17:37.51,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,The victim Seiji-san was\N22 years old at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.92,0:17:41.32,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,He received education for\Ngifted children from a young age,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.32,0:17:46.54,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,and he was to work for his father's\Ncompany once he graduated from college.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.35,0:17:51.64,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,As the heir to Koike Real Estate,\Nexpectations for him were high,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.64,0:17:56.21,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,and people said he possessed\Nthe talent to meet them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.24,0:18:01.72,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,According to witnesses, despite\Nliving at the same mansion,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.72,0:18:04.90,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,they shared hardly any connections.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.64,0:18:10.44,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Someone even said they'd never\Nseen them speak to one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.44,0:18:16.20,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,So the culprit's resentment\Ncame from unfounded assumptions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:17.03,0:18:18.91,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,The moon and the sun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.99,0:18:26.88,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,The victim Seiji was Koike Tatsuya's\Nheir and had a promising future.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.41,0:18:31.76,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, the culprit was the gardener's\Nson and a poorly-behaved problem child.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.23,0:18:35.00,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,I can imagine what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.00,0:18:39.29,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,But that still doesn't explain\Nwhy he'd kill three people he knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.64,0:18:43.21,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,What are we supposed to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.16,0:18:48.24,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,We have a rough picture\Nof the 20-year-old case.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.24,0:18:54.65,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,But what does it have to do\Nwith Detective Mihashi's murder?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.00,0:18:57.64,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Don't worry. We're getting close.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.53,0:19:04.15,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,The culprit set a fire\Nto hide something, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.15,0:19:10.04,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Since they did it in a hurry, you\Nmust be getting close to the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.63,0:19:15.04,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I bet that while Mihashi-san was\Ninvestigating this case,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.04,0:19:19.43,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,he learned something the culprit\Ndidn't want him to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.43,0:19:22.18,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,That's certainly possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.18,0:19:26.51,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,But this is all information\Nreported in the news.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.51,0:19:30.19,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,What could the culprit be trying to hide?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.64,0:19:34.57,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Don't we need to keep\Ninvestigating to find out?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.57,0:19:37.00,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.00,0:19:40.58,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,But all our clues went up in flames.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.05,0:19:45.00,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,But we know where to go next.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.00,0:19:46.37,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Right, Mister?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.50,0:19:51.93,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,If this wedding hall is\Nthe key connecting these cases,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.93,0:19:55.96,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,we should talk to Koike-san,\Nwho had it built.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.96,0:19:58.51,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Isn't that what you're thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.51,0:20:01.39,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Huh? Uh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.74,0:20:04.13,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,That may be difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.10,0:20:06.64,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.31,0:20:10.69,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Koike Tatsuya, president\Nof Koike Real Estate
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.69,0:20:13.73,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,and father of the victim\Nin the 20-year-old case,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.73,0:20:16.28,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,passed away three months ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.98,0:20:18.15,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.52,0:20:22.78,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,No, there was no foul play.\NHe died of an illness.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.69,0:20:25.16,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,So we've hit a dead end.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.43,0:20:26.96,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,No, not yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.32,0:20:28.87,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.87,0:20:32.34,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Haven't you heard the saying,\N"Dead men tell no tales?"
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.34,0:20:35.35,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,I have, but look.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.13,0:20:40.51,sign_1220_phone_messages,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\fscx80\bord4\3c&HFFFDFE&\fnGeorgia\b1\fs12\an8\pos(324,66)}DEATH OF PRESIDENT\NKOIKE TATSUYA\NOF KOIKE REAL ESTATE
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.51,0:20:40.51,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,It says his wife Toshiko-san\Nrepresented the family at the funeral.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.90,0:20:45.39,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,I see. We can ask the wife\Nwhat things were like back then.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.39,0:20:46.39,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.90,0:20:52.27,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,She must know something\Nsince she lost her son.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.27,0:20:54.33,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Let's go, Mori-san.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.28,0:20:56.28,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.41,0:21:09.35,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Wh-What a mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.35,0:21:12.70,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,One fit for a real estate mogul.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.70,0:21:14.30,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.93,0:21:16.81,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.42,0:21:19.67,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,What are you doing over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.55,0:21:24.93,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,What are you all doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.93,0:21:31.35,sign_song_ed_1214,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an1\q2\pos(45,280)\blur0.2\fad(500,1)}Ai de Zenbu Dakishimete Aishite\N\NSong by Kuraki Mai
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.93,0:22:54.56,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Just so you know, this is {\i1}our{\i0} case.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.01,0:22:58.06,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Stay out of our way.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.06,0:23:00.94,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,Wait, why is she pointing at {\i0}me{\i1}?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.29,0:23:05.82,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,We're not playing around, miss.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.82,0:23:09.14,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Right back at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.14,0:23:11.46,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,We're not playing around, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.46,0:23:14.58,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,We've been officially hired.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.58,0:23:15.96,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Hired?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.25,0:23:19.34,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,Hired? Who hired you?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.67,0:23:21.29,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Isn't it obvious?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.29,0:23:23.88,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,We were officially hired\Nby the woman who lives here,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.88,0:23:27.09,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Koike Toshiko-san, to investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.90,0:23:31.93,DCMain,SONOKO,0,0,0,,Because we are the Five Detective Girls!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.47,0:23:35.35,sign_1220_detective_girls_1,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an2\pos(320,225)\fad(300,600)}\hFIVE\h\hDETECTIVE\h\hGIRLS\h
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.35,0:23:37.12,DCMain,CHIBA,0,0,0,,Five...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.12,0:23:38.60,DCMain,TAKAGI,0,0,0,,...Detective...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.60,0:23:39.98,DCMain,KOGORO,0,0,0,,...Girls?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.33,0:23:42.59,DCMain,CONAN,0,0,0,,What kind of name is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.99,0:24:09.01,sign_episode_preview,SIGN,0,0,0,,Episode Preview
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.99,0:23:46.99,DCMain,ALL,0,0,0,,A secret child?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.33,0:23:51.66,DCItalic,CONAN/ID,0,0,0,,An infidelity investigation\Nand a secret child. Could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:51.66,0:23:55.16,DCMain,SATO,0,0,0,,How would you describe Tatsuya-san?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.48,0:23:59.79,DCMain,TOSHIKO,0,0,0,,I'd say he was a naughty fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.79,0:24:01.54,DCMain,ALL,0,0,0,,An enemy to women everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.07,0:24:08.33,DCMain,ALL,0,0,0,,Thrilling Five Detective\NGirls High School!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.80,0:24:09.01,sign_1220_detective_girls_2,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,18)\fad(300,1)\an2}THRILLING
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.80,0:24:09.01,sign_1220_detective_girls_3,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an2\blur.03\pos(320,250)\fad(300,1)\bord4\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H8F61A5&}5 Detective Girls
Dialogue: 1,0:24:07.80,0:24:09.01,sign_1220_detective_girls_3,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an2\blur.03\pos(320,250)\fad(300,1)}5 Detective Girls
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.01,0:24:15.02,sign_next_episode,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,45)}Girls Day Mystery 5\N(Part Two)
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.44,0:24:14.17,DCItalic,CONAN,0,0,0,,The next episode of Conan is\N"Girls Day Mystery 5, Part Two!"
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.03,0:24:34.95,sign_hint_label,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an2\fnImpact\pos(320,300)}{\c&H0E0F16&}{\3c&HA9A5A4&}\h{\3c&HAEABA9&}\h{\3c&HB5B1AF&}\h{\3c&HB5B1AF&}\h{\3c&HBAB4B3&}T{\3c&HB5B1AF&}H{\3c&HC9BCBC&}E{\3c&HCFC5C0&}\h{\3c&HCFC5C0&}M{\3c&HC9BCBC&}O{\3c&HB5B1AF&}O{\3c&HA8A4A3&}N{\3c&HACA7A5&}\h{\3c&HACA7A5&}\h{\3c&HADA9A8&}\h{\3c&HB5ABAA&}\h\N{\3c&HA9A5A4&}\h{\3c&HB1AEAC&}A{\3c&HBAB4B3&}N{\3c&HC9C2C1&}D{\3c&HD1CAC9&}\h{\3c&HDFD9D8&}T{\3c&HECE8E6&}H{\3c&HE6E0E0&}E{\3c&HD6CBC7&}\h{\3c&HCBC5C3&}S{\3c&HC3BEBC&}U{\3c&HB5B1AF&}N{\3c&HBEB5B4&}\h
Dialogue: 0,0:24:30.78,0:24:32.80,DCItalicTop,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Next Conan's hint!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.80,0:24:34.95,DCItalicTop,CONAN,0,0,0,,The moon and the sun!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.95,0:24:39.96,sign_dont_miss,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\pos(245,304)}Don't miss the next episode.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.95,0:24:36.93,DCMainTop,KOGORO,0,0,0,,Well, {\i1}we're{\i0} the Four Detective Boys!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.93,0:24:37.50,DCMainTop,TAKAGI & CHIBA,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.50,0:24:38.65,DCMainTop,CONAN,0,0,0,,What?

